### Todo Management API - end-to-end smoke test
### Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or JetBrains HTTP client.
### Run top to bottom. Variables carry between requests.

@base = http://localhost:8080

### Health
GET {{base}}/health

### Register user A
# @name registerA
POST {{base}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Alice Example",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Register user A again -> 409
POST {{base}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Alice", "email": "alice@example.com", "password": "password123" }

### Register with bad input -> 400 with errors map
POST {{base}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "x", "email": "not-an-email", "password": "short" }

### Login user A (captures token)
# @name loginA
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@example.com", "password": "password123" }

@tokenA = {{loginA.response.body.data.token}}

### Access todos without a token -> 401
GET {{base}}/api/todos

### Create a category
# @name category
POST {{base}}/api/categories
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

{ "name": "Work" }

@categoryId = {{category.response.body.data.id}}

### Create todo 1
# @name todo1
POST {{base}}/api/todos
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

{
  "title": "Complete backend assignment",
  "description": "Develop Todo APIs using Golang and Fiber",
  "status": "pending",
  "priority": "high",
  "due_date": "2026-09-15",
  "category_ids": [{{categoryId}}]
}

@todoId = {{todo1.response.body.data.id}}

### Create todo 2
POST {{base}}/api/todos
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

{ "title": "Write README", "priority": "medium", "status": "in_progress" }

### Create todo 3
POST {{base}}/api/todos
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

{ "title": "Ship it", "priority": "low", "status": "pending", "due_date": "2026-10-01" }

### List page 1, limit 2
GET {{base}}/api/todos?page=1&limit=2&sort=created_at&order=desc
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

### Filter: pending + high
GET {{base}}/api/todos?status=pending&priority=high
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

### Search by title
GET {{base}}/api/todos?search=backend
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

### Get todo by id
GET {{base}}/api/todos/{{todoId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

### Update todo
PUT {{base}}/api/todos/{{todoId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

{ "title": "Complete backend assignment (revised)", "priority": "medium" }

### Patch status
PATCH {{base}}/api/todos/{{todoId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

{ "status": "completed" }

### Register user B
# @name loginB
POST {{base}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Bob Example", "email": "bob@example.com", "password": "password123" }

### Login user B
# @name loginBauth
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "bob@example.com", "password": "password123" }

@tokenB = {{loginBauth.response.body.data.token}}

### User B tries to read user A's todo -> 404
GET {{base}}/api/todos/{{todoId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenB}}

### Delete (soft) todo as user A
DELETE {{base}}/api/todos/{{todoId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}

### Confirm it's gone from the list
GET {{base}}/api/todos
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenA}}
